{# Feed count resync partial — rendered by GET /feed/count on SSE (re)connect.
   Outputs the M span (#feed-lot-count) plus OOB swaps for #registry-count (X)
   and #header-status. Requires lot_count (M), active_lot_count (X), and
   monitor (VM namespace) in context.
   Note: monitor.state reflects the DB/session snapshot at reconnect time
   (awaiting_backfill / active / warning / error). The transient "checking"
   state lives only seconds and is not represented in the VM — a reconnect
   during a check will briefly show "active" until the next SseStatus event.

   SYNC NOTE: the #header-status div attributes below (id, hx-swap-oob, class,
   sse-swap, role, aria-label) MUST match base.html.jinja#header-status exactly.
   sse-swap="status" is load-bearing — htmx uses it to re-subscribe the SSE
   event listener after the OOB swap. Any divergence breaks SSE status updates.
   See also: base.html.jinja#header-status / _feed_count_resync.html.jinja — keep in sync. #}
{% include 'partials/_feed_lot_count.html.jinja' %}
<span id="registry-count"
      hx-swap-oob="true"
      class="js-registry-count"
      data-count="{{ active_lot_count }}">{{ active_lot_count }}</span>
<div id="header-status"
     hx-swap-oob="true"
     class="header__center"
     sse-swap="status"
     role="region"
     aria-label="Статус мониторинга">{% include "partials/_header_status.html.jinja" %}</div>
